<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carloman (mayor of the palace)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 710–754</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carloman was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a> and Frankish mayor of the palace in Austrasia from 741 to 747, ruling jointly with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-the-short">Pepin the Short</a>. He campaigned against the Alemanni, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavarians">Bavarians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a>, crushing Alemannic resistance at Cannstatt in 746, and supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-boniface">Saint Boniface</a>'s reform of the Frankish church. In 747 he renounced power and became a monk in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, at Monte Soracte and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monte-cassino">Monte Cassino</a>.</p></div>
